# HTTP response headers for the WEB deploy (Netlify / Cloudflare Pages format).
# Applies ONLY to the hosted web build — Electron, Android, and iOS do not read
# this file (they get their own CSP: Electron via main.cjs; mobile via WebView
# config). Keeping the web CSP here avoids one shared meta-CSP over-restricting a
# native platform we can't smoke-test headlessly.
#
# NOTE ON HOSTS: GitHub Pages does NOT support custom headers, so on bare Pages
# this file is ignored and the CSP is NOT delivered. Netlify and Cloudflare Pages
# apply it natively. See docs/release/WEB_DEPLOY_CHECKLIST.md.
#
# The script-src sha256 below is the hash of the inline boot/touch-gate script in
# index.html. If that inline script changes, this hash MUST be regenerated
# (tests/release/cspHash.test.mjs fails until it matches). Regenerate with:
#   node -e 'const f=require("fs"),c=require("crypto");const m=f.readFileSync("index.html","utf8").match(/<script>([\s\S]*?)<\/script>/);console.log("sha256-"+c.createHash("sha256").update(m[1]).digest("base64"))'

